    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44667" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπαίδ-ευτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well-educated,
			well-trained</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				43
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				410
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἄλλων -ότατοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Piet.</u>
					65
				</span></i>
			; <i>docile</i>, of an elephant, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				2.11
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπαίδευτόν ἐστι</span> it is
				<i>a thing easily learnt</i>, c. inf., <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ἐπιστολή</span> a
				<i>scholarly</i> letter, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Pomp.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CD</u>
				1.3
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότερον</span> Athenoclesap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				5.177e
			</span></i>.</div>
